{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>לְמַעַן יַאֲרִיכוּן.</b> He said <b>יַאֲרִיכוּן</b>, which means of themselves, and He did not say ״I shall lengthen your days.״ Or perhaps it intends to say that this commandment — its inherent property is length of days aside from its reward from HaShem, for there are commandments that have wondrous inherent properties besides the reward that HaShem established for them, and this one HaShem revealed."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:31:04.710542967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}